From 7c1e0b3a9d5f2e8c4b6a1d0f9e8c7b6a5d4c3b2a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Petr=20=C5=A0tetiar?= <petr.stetiar@prplfoundation.org>
Date: Thu, 25 Sep 2026 10:30:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] AP MLD: Drop the borrowed driver context when a link add
 fails

A non-first link BSS of an AP MLD does not get a driver context of its
own. hostapd_setup_bss() (src/ap/hostapd.c:1496-1498) and, for the
first BSS of a later interface, hostapd_driver_init()
(hostapd/main.c:178-180) copy hapd->drv_priv and hapd->interface_added
from the first BSS of the MLD (hostapd_mld_get_first_bss()) and jump to
setup_mld, where hostapd_drv_link_add() registers the new link with the
driver and, only if that succeeds, hostapd_mld_add_link() puts the BSS
on mld->links (hostapd.c:1542-1549, main.c:343-350).

If hostapd_drv_link_add() fails, both functions return -1 with the
borrowed pointers still in place. The BSS then looks like a fully
initialized link to every later consumer, although the driver has no
record of it and mld->links does not list it:

 - The failed-BSS unwind in hostapd_setup_interface_complete_sync()
   (hostapd.c:2680-2690) runs hostapd_bss_deinit_no_free() on it, which
   flushes/deauthenticates through the sibling's i802_bss and, because
   interface_added was copied too, calls hostapd_if_remove() ->
   hostapd_if_link_remove() on the sibling's context with a link ID the
   driver never accepted (hostapd.c:551-565, ap_drv_ops.c:616-629).
   nl80211 rejects the unknown link (driver_nl80211.c:10941-10943),
   so hapd->drv_priv is left as it was.

 - When that setup ran asynchronously (channel list update, ACS, DFS),
   the failing interface is not freed: it goes to HAPD_IFACE_DISABLED
   (hostapd.c:2797-2827) and stays in interfaces->iface[] with the
   failed BSS still pointing at the sibling's i802_bss.

 - When the sibling is later torn down, its i802_bss is freed by
   wpa_driver_nl80211_deinit() (driver->hapd_deinit(), reached from
   hostapd_cleanup_driver(), hostapd.c:3506-3517) or by
   wpa_driver_nl80211_if_remove() (last link removed,
   driver_nl80211.c:10960-10970). The only invalidation of the
   borrowers, hostapd_mld_interface_freed() (hostapd.c:5109-5117),
   walks mld->links, so the failed BSS keeps a dangling pointer.

 - On TERMINATE, hostapd_interface_deinit() of the disabled interface
   calls hostapd_bss_deinit_no_free() -> hostapd_flush_old_stations()
   -> hostapd_drv_sta_deauth() on that BSS. The existing
   hapd->drv_priv == NULL guards (hostapd.c:842, ap_drv_ops.c:905) do
   not help because the pointer is not NULL, just freed;
   i802_sta_deauth() dereferences it (bss->drv, driver_nl80211.c:8389)
   and crashes.

Observed with a warm per-link ADD on a mac80211 AP MLD: the interface
waited in COUNTRY_UPDATE, then "MLD: Failed to add link 3 in MLD
wlan2.2" / "Interface initialization failed" / "wlan2.1: interface
state COUNTRY_UPDATE->DISABLED"; ~15 s later the MLD's owning
interface was removed ("nl80211: deinit ifname=wlan2.2") and the
subsequent TERMINATE segfaulted in i802_sta_deauth()+0x21 with a heap
fault address while deinitializing the disabled interface ("wlan2.1:
interface state DISABLED->DISABLED").

Fix it at the failure point: when hostapd_drv_link_add() fails for a
BSS that borrowed its driver context, clear hapd->drv_priv and
hapd->interface_added before returning. The failed BSS never owned or
registered anything in the driver, so there is nothing to release; the
existing NULL guards in hostapd_flush_old_stations(),
hostapd_if_remove()/hostapd_if_link_remove() and the hostapd_drv_*()
wrappers then make the unwind and any later deinit a no-op for it. A
BSS that obtained its own context through hostapd_if_add() on this path
is left untouched so that its context is still released by the regular
cleanup.

hostap.git HEAD 5401e02628f9 (2026-09-25) has the same bare "return -1"
at both sites (src/ap/hostapd.c:1577-1583, hostapd/main.c:387-393) and
the same mld->links-only hostapd_mld_interface_freed().

Signed-off-by: Petr Štetiar <petr.stetiar@prplfoundation.org>
---
 hostapd/main.c   |  6 ++++++
 src/ap/hostapd.c | 17 +++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 23 insertions(+)

diff --git a/hostapd/main.c b/hostapd/main.c
--- a/hostapd/main.c
+++ b/hostapd/main.c
@@ -345,6 +345,12 @@ setup_mld:
 			wpa_printf(MSG_ERROR,
 				   "MLD: Failed to add link %d in MLD %s",
 				   hapd->mld_link_id, hapd->conf->iface);
+			/* Same as in hostapd_setup_bss(): drop a borrowed driver
+			 * context that this link never got registered with. */
+			if (h_hapd) {
+				hapd->drv_priv = NULL;
+				hapd->interface_added = 0;
+			}
 			return -1;
 		}
 		hostapd_mld_add_link(hapd);
diff --git a/src/ap/hostapd.c b/src/ap/hostapd.c
--- a/src/ap/hostapd.c
+++ b/src/ap/hostapd.c
@@ -1442,6 +1442,9 @@ int hostapd_setup_bss(struct hostapd_dat
 	char force_ifname[IFNAMSIZ];
 	u8 if_addr[ETH_ALEN];
 	int flush_old_stations = 1;
+#ifdef CONFIG_IEEE80211BE
+	bool drv_priv_borrowed = false;
+#endif /* CONFIG_IEEE80211BE */
 
 	if (!hostapd_mld_is_first_bss(hapd))
 		wpa_printf(MSG_DEBUG,
@@ -1496,6 +1499,7 @@ int hostapd_setup_bss(struct hostapd_dat
 			if (h_hapd) {
 				hapd->drv_priv = h_hapd->drv_priv;
 				hapd->interface_added = h_hapd->interface_added;
+				drv_priv_borrowed = true;
 				wpa_printf(MSG_DEBUG,
 					   "Setup of non first link (%d) BSS of MLD %s",
 					   hapd->mld_link_id, hapd->conf->iface);
@@ -1544,6 +1548,19 @@ setup_mld:
 			wpa_printf(MSG_ERROR,
 				   "MLD: Failed to add link %d in MLD %s",
 				   hapd->mld_link_id, hapd->conf->iface);
+			/* The driver context was borrowed from the first BSS of
+			 * the AP MLD and this link was never added to it, so
+			 * the failed BSS neither owns nor references anything
+			 * in the driver. Drop the borrowed pointers so that
+			 * the cleanup does not deauthenticate/remove on behalf
+			 * of the sibling and, more importantly, so that no
+			 * stale pointer remains once the sibling frees its
+			 * context: hostapd_mld_interface_freed() can only
+			 * invalidate links that made it onto mld->links. */
+			if (drv_priv_borrowed) {
+				hapd->drv_priv = NULL;
+				hapd->interface_added = 0;
+			}
 			return -1;
 		}
 		hostapd_mld_add_link(hapd);
